{"id": "en_tornado_home_p1", "total": 64.91, "segments": [{"text": "If a tornado warning hits, do not stay in a car or a mobile home.", "start": 0.0, "end": 3.32}, {"text": "Sam sees dark spinning clouds above his house with 2 minutes before impact.", "start": 3.58, "end": 6.56}, {"text": "The roaring tornado slams into the sturdy building, shattering glass and outer walls.", "start": 6.96, "end": 10.7}, {"text": "Sam rushes downstairs and goes straight inside the underground basement shelter for safety.", "start": 11.38, "end": 14.64}, {"text": "One. Go to the basement, or an interior room on the lowest floor with no windows.", "start": 15.14, "end": 18.64}, {"text": "Sam secures himself in the dark basement as loud warning sirens blare outside.", "start": 19.24, "end": 22.3}, {"text": "Two. Put as many walls as possible between your body and the storm outside.", "start": 22.84, "end": 26.0}, {"text": "He retreats deeper into the corner, placing thick walls between himself and exterior doors.", "start": 26.0, "end": 30.26}, {"text": "Three. Cover your head and neck with your arms, a mattress or helmets.", "start": 30.8, "end": 33.94}, {"text": "Sam pulls a heavy mattress over his head and drops down into a crouch.", "start": 34.64, "end": 37.2}, {"text": "Cars and mobile homes are not safe, so hiding in this sturdy building protects him.", "start": 37.78, "end": 40.98}, {"text": "The entire home shakes violently while terrifying flying debris impacts the upper structure.", "start": 41.38, "end": 45.48}, {"text": "Heavy wind roars wildly above while the tornado passes directly over his safe position.", "start": 45.94, "end": 49.76}, {"text": "Sam follows every official safety rule to withstand this dangerous extreme weather disaster.", "start": 50.3, "end": 54.14}, {"text": "It was the perfect plan to survive the storm. There was just one problem.", "start": 54.14, "end": 57.4}, {"text": "An outer basement window shatters, blowing glass and roaring wind directly int